{
  "name": "Universe Forge",
  "icon": "theoreticalsciences:universe_forge",
  "category": "theoreticalsciences:strings",
  "sortnum": 42,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:universe_forge",
      "title": "Universe Forge",
      "text": "Triggers false-vacuum decay and cosmic inflation to grow - and later harvest - a pocket universe. I have never been more nervous.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 5$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Note to self: this controller is too complex for a crafting grid. It has to be built on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts before ordering anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "A $(thing)false vacuum$() is a metastable state; if it decays, a bubble of true vacuum expands at nearly light speed. $(thing)Inflation$(), driven by the inflaton field, stretched our universe by a factor of at least 10^26 in a fraction of a second. Combine them and you get a universe in a box."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Procedure: first forge a $(item)Pocket Universe$() from a $(item)Universe Seed$(), $(fluid)False Vacuum$() and $(fluid)Inflaton Field$(). Then feed it back in to harvest it until only a $(item)Heat Death Remnant$() remains.$(br2)Four remnants can be re-inflated into a new seed. Nothing is wasted, not even the end of time."
    },
